    feat: boot SAVE block reads freshest /game/save/current (DF-AIPP-5)
    
    The boot SAVE block previously rendered only /game/save/{party,items,location}.
    It now also fetches the freshest /game/save/current record (the run-truth
    distillation key written by MEM-3; duckbrain_client.get() already returns the
    most recent active record) and renders one "- current:" line via a defensive
    renderer: map/pos/party hints when present, otherwise a <=200-char fallback
    body/JSON dump; absent or empty record leaves the output unchanged (the
    byte-identical placeholder path is preserved when the store is empty).
    
    Stale marathon_driver.py references: none exist in this repo (verified across
    all commits) - the stale refs live in fleet skills, out of worker scope.
    
    Verified: pytest tests/test_boot_memory_injection.py 14 passed (4 new),
    ruff clean, mypy 0 errors, scripts/backfill_runs.py --dry-run exit 0, and a
    live boot render showed "- current: Oak's Lab (map 40) at 3,2; 1 party member(s)".
    
    Addresses DF-AIPP-5.
    
    Co-authored-by: Alexis Okuwa <wojonstech@gmail.com>
